WEBVTT

00:00:14.760 --> 00:00:22.560
"Taisho Otome Fairy Tale"

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:32.050
"Taisho Otome Fairy Tale"

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:37.010
"Episode 12"
"A Spring Storm"

00:01:46.350 --> 00:01:47.850
It's so cold...

00:01:50.940 --> 00:01:56.570
I just want to get back to
Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>... soon.

00:02:02.870 --> 00:02:04.040
Momma!

00:02:07.910 --> 00:02:09.210
Momma!

00:02:15.510 --> 00:02:16.970
Momma...

00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:20.180
Yuzu.

00:02:20.180 --> 00:02:28.230
When I had you, I wanted you to be
the happiest in the whole world.

00:02:28.230 --> 00:02:31.810
So from here on out, no matter what,

00:02:31.810 --> 00:02:35.030
turn toward joy.

00:02:35.030 --> 00:02:37.360
Momma...

00:02:37.360 --> 00:02:42.620
You'd been telling me that since
I was a little girl, Momma.

00:02:44.580 --> 00:02:49.040
"Midorigawa Academy"

00:02:44.580 --> 00:02:49.040
I'm sorry for just up
and leaving you like that.

00:02:49.040 --> 00:02:54.000
But when I heard Poppa was
on the hook for Uncle's debts,

00:02:54.000 --> 00:02:57.050
I knew I had to do something.

00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:11.980
You'll be looking after my son.

00:03:11.980 --> 00:03:15.480
He lost the use of his
right hand in an accident.

00:03:15.480 --> 00:03:20.150
Do you know the saying
"A child is an everlasting burden"?

00:03:20.150 --> 00:03:24.410
That's my useless child, all right:
a shackle around my neck.

00:03:24.410 --> 00:03:26.740
The Shima family has no need of him.

00:03:32.790 --> 00:03:35.840
What terrible treatment
must he have endured?

00:03:40.050 --> 00:03:43.010
Don't want to catch a cold.

00:03:43.010 --> 00:03:49.770
This man--Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>...
I'm sure he'll cherish me.

00:03:49.770 --> 00:03:52.440
I'll be by his side for always.

00:03:53.440 --> 00:03:56.770
Please don't worry, Momma.

00:03:56.770 --> 00:04:02.450
Thanks to the clumsy kindness
Tamahiko-<i>sama </i>shows me,

00:04:02.450 --> 00:04:07.580
I'm constantly surrounded
by toasty-warm feelings.

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:10.700
Someday, I too...

00:04:11.660 --> 00:04:15.500
The bellflower means
"unchanging love," doesn't it?

00:04:15.500 --> 00:04:17.420
Then no matter what this looks like,

00:04:17.420 --> 00:04:19.960
the sentiment remains the same!

00:04:21.300 --> 00:04:23.970
That's... what I think.

00:04:23.970 --> 00:04:27.720
I might tell him how I feel.

00:04:29.930 --> 00:04:32.230
Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>...

00:04:32.230 --> 00:04:35.100
I think I... I...

00:04:39.610 --> 00:04:41.690
Um, Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>?

00:04:41.690 --> 00:04:44.030
Hmm? What is it?

00:04:45.070 --> 00:04:46.950
Oh, um, nothing.

00:04:50.540 --> 00:04:56.580
Normally I'd blurt out whatever
it is I wanted to say.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:04.340
All this biting my tongue
is starting to hurt.

00:05:06.180 --> 00:05:09.220
I'll tell Tamahiko-<i>sama </i>on his birthday.

00:05:09.220 --> 00:05:12.270
If I can't <i>say </i>it, I can
at least put it in a letter.

00:05:17.060 --> 00:05:23.110
My timidity kept me from writing
what I really wanted to say.

00:05:24.690 --> 00:05:27.660
We <i>will </i>be husband and wife eventually.

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:30.450
Maybe we don't need those words.

00:05:31.530 --> 00:05:34.080
But I still want to tell him.

00:05:34.080 --> 00:05:38.420
I want Tamahiko-<i>sama </i>to know how I feel.

00:05:38.420 --> 00:05:39.670
And yet...

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:45.760
Yuzuki-<i>san</i>... you go. Leave me here.

00:05:45.760 --> 00:05:47.220
I can't!

00:05:47.220 --> 00:05:51.930
We'll... we'll make it
back together. I know it.

00:05:51.930 --> 00:05:53.970
Back to our loved ones!

00:06:00.020 --> 00:06:01.230
Midori-<i>san</i>!

00:06:03.230 --> 00:06:04.650
Yuzuki-<i>san</i>!

00:06:15.200 --> 00:06:17.870
No matter what happens, I have to survive.

00:06:19.920 --> 00:06:21.250
I miss him...

00:06:31.180 --> 00:06:32.680
Wow!

00:06:36.730 --> 00:06:43.230
♬ In the moonless sky I see them ♬

00:06:43.230 --> 00:06:47.780
♬ Tiny lights that twinkle so ♬

00:06:49.780 --> 00:06:56.700
♬ There, in those starry shadows ♬

00:06:56.700 --> 00:07:00.790
♬ See the shape of hope aglow ♬

00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:06.840
Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>...

00:07:06.840 --> 00:07:08.210
I miss you.

00:07:09.260 --> 00:07:10.550
Sis?

00:07:10.550 --> 00:07:12.140
Big Sis Yuzuki?

00:07:23.480 --> 00:07:27.230
I'm sorry, Momma.

00:07:27.230 --> 00:07:32.990
I... might not be able to be
the happiest in the whole world.

00:07:42.370 --> 00:07:43.380
Yuzu...

00:07:44.330 --> 00:07:45.630
Yuzu!

00:07:52.720 --> 00:07:57.220
I wanted us to celebrate
your birthday together this year.

00:08:05.610 --> 00:08:09.780
If this is what it comes to,
I should have told you how I felt.

00:08:14.700 --> 00:08:16.280
Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>...

00:08:16.280 --> 00:08:19.620
If I could have one wish--
just a glimpse of him...

00:08:21.500 --> 00:08:22.910
Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>!

00:08:24.790 --> 00:08:26.040
Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>!

00:08:29.050 --> 00:08:30.710
Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>...

00:08:31.720 --> 00:08:33.300
Yuzu!

00:08:33.300 --> 00:08:35.010
Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>!

00:08:35.010 --> 00:08:36.760
Yuzu!

00:08:36.760 --> 00:08:38.180
Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>!

00:08:39.220 --> 00:08:41.640
Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>!

00:08:47.980 --> 00:08:49.480
Yuzu!

00:08:49.480 --> 00:08:51.740
Yuzu... Yuzu!

00:08:56.070 --> 00:08:59.620
Yuzu... at last--thank God...

00:09:02.080 --> 00:09:02.910
Ta...

00:09:08.040 --> 00:09:11.210
It's all right. It's all right, Yuzu.

00:09:11.210 --> 00:09:12.960
You did great.

00:09:15.010 --> 00:09:17.090
Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>...

00:09:17.090 --> 00:09:19.390
Yes--it's me. I'm right here.

00:09:19.390 --> 00:09:21.720
Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>...

00:09:34.610 --> 00:09:36.650
I love you.

00:09:36.650 --> 00:09:39.820
I love you <i>so much</i>!

00:09:42.870 --> 00:09:44.950
I-I know!

00:09:44.950 --> 00:09:48.790
Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>, I <i>love </i>you!

00:09:48.790 --> 00:09:51.040
We're, uh... we're not at home.

00:09:57.550 --> 00:10:00.300
It's a little late to be so mortified.

00:10:00.300 --> 00:10:02.600
Um... where are we?

00:10:02.600 --> 00:10:05.980
The third-class waiting
room at Tokyo Station.

00:10:05.980 --> 00:10:11.190
It's a first-aid site--hospitals
throughout the city have burned down.

00:10:11.190 --> 00:10:12.730
Oh, I see...

00:10:14.570 --> 00:10:18.280
Wh-Where's Midori-<i>san</i>? And those children!

00:10:18.280 --> 00:10:21.490
Midori-<i>san </i>is at the
Ueno maternity clinic.

00:10:21.490 --> 00:10:24.540
She's gotten in touch with her partner.

00:10:24.540 --> 00:10:27.540
Her baby's all right, too.

00:10:27.540 --> 00:10:29.540
So are Yoko and Shinyu!

00:10:29.540 --> 00:10:31.710
Thank goodness...

00:10:31.710 --> 00:10:33.630
Wait--huh?

00:10:33.630 --> 00:10:35.380
What's everyone doing <i>here</i>?!

00:10:35.380 --> 00:10:38.220
Long time no see, sis!

00:10:38.220 --> 00:10:41.720
I'm here contributing to the aid effort,
helping out my uncle.

00:10:44.390 --> 00:10:49.020
Tamasuke Manabe. Thank you
for taking care of my nephew.

00:10:49.020 --> 00:10:50.940
No, thank <i>you</i>.

00:10:50.940 --> 00:10:53.940
Um... I'm Yuzuki.

00:10:53.940 --> 00:10:59.900
To be seeing you here, Yuzu--
<i>and </i>Kotori-<i>chan</i>? What a thrill!

00:11:03.030 --> 00:11:06.040
You still need to rest quietly, Yuzu.

00:11:06.040 --> 00:11:06.870
Ryo-<i>san</i>!

00:11:06.870 --> 00:11:09.580
And who are <i>you </i>in this equation?

00:11:09.580 --> 00:11:11.120
Who, me?

00:11:11.120 --> 00:11:13.540
I'm Yuzu and Tamahiko's friend.

00:11:13.540 --> 00:11:14.960
"Friend"?!

00:11:14.960 --> 00:11:17.710
Don't get too buddy-buddy with Yuzu, now!

00:11:17.710 --> 00:11:19.840
<i>I'm </i>the one taking care of her!

00:11:19.840 --> 00:11:23.390
And <i>you'd </i>better watch
how you talk to people!

00:11:23.390 --> 00:11:26.470
Besides, my brother--a friend?
Not in a million years.

00:11:26.470 --> 00:11:27.470
"Daaang!"

00:11:26.470 --> 00:11:27.470
What?!

00:11:28.180 --> 00:11:30.640
They'll get along like gangbusters!

00:11:30.640 --> 00:11:33.190
Me and Shima-<i>kun </i>are friends, too!

00:11:35.190 --> 00:11:37.030
<i>Stare</i>...

00:11:38.860 --> 00:11:39.900
What is it?

00:11:39.900 --> 00:11:43.950
You... you really came.

00:11:43.950 --> 00:11:45.530
For me.

00:11:47.120 --> 00:11:48.160
Uh-huh.

00:11:49.660 --> 00:11:51.040
Oh, right!

00:11:51.040 --> 00:11:54.250
Here, Yuzu: rice porridge. Want some?

00:11:55.840 --> 00:11:56.920
I do!

00:12:19.030 --> 00:12:20.820
It's delicious.

00:12:20.820 --> 00:12:26.240
I thought I might never
be able to eat again...

00:12:26.240 --> 00:12:29.870
Eat up and get well soon, okay?

00:12:29.870 --> 00:12:31.540
Okay.

00:12:31.540 --> 00:12:32.830
Doctor Manabe?

00:12:35.040 --> 00:12:37.340
You have visitors.

00:12:37.340 --> 00:12:38.340
Father?!

00:12:41.800 --> 00:12:43.800
And my sister... Tamayo...

00:12:43.800 --> 00:12:46.800
It's been a while, Tamasuke.

00:12:46.800 --> 00:12:48.760
Brother!

00:12:48.760 --> 00:12:50.850
What are <i>you </i>doing here?

00:12:50.850 --> 00:12:55.980
When I telephoned your clinic,
I was told you were in Tokyo.

00:12:55.980 --> 00:12:57.810
Excellent timing.

00:12:57.810 --> 00:13:00.610
Tamaki was injured in the quake.

00:13:00.610 --> 00:13:02.030
My brother was?

00:13:02.030 --> 00:13:05.160
Let the other doctors handle all... this.

00:13:05.160 --> 00:13:07.070
<i>You </i>come with <i>me</i>.

00:13:08.910 --> 00:13:10.870
How dare you?

00:13:10.870 --> 00:13:13.500
I'm not a Shima anymore.

00:13:13.500 --> 00:13:14.750
Please leave!

00:13:14.750 --> 00:13:17.170
For someone not in the Shima family,

00:13:17.170 --> 00:13:21.840
you certainly seem awfully friendly
with Tamahiko and Tamako.

00:13:27.680 --> 00:13:30.310
What is Tamahiko doing here?

00:13:30.310 --> 00:13:33.020
I believe I told you he was dead to us.

00:13:33.020 --> 00:13:35.560
Are you still going on about that?

00:13:35.560 --> 00:13:40.400
Tamahiko walked here from Chiba
for Yuzuki-<i>san</i>, lost in the quake--

00:13:40.400 --> 00:13:43.650
someone who truly cares for him.

00:13:43.650 --> 00:13:48.620
He's left you behind and is
finally coming into his own!

00:13:48.620 --> 00:13:50.660
Tamahiko has grown stronger.

00:13:53.830 --> 00:13:57.120
I've written you a referral. Try there.

00:14:01.460 --> 00:14:03.130
Let's go, Tamayo.

00:14:03.130 --> 00:14:05.340
Oh, are you sure?

00:14:05.340 --> 00:14:08.340
Then farewell, all! Get well soon.

00:14:13.520 --> 00:14:14.640
Father!

00:14:20.730 --> 00:14:22.440
I'm glad you're all right.

00:14:29.490 --> 00:14:33.370
We stayed in Tokyo for a while after that,

00:14:33.370 --> 00:14:35.540
helping my uncle with his work

00:14:35.540 --> 00:14:37.830
and seeing so many smiling faces again.

00:14:40.460 --> 00:14:45.090
"Aiding the nation begins near at hand.

00:14:45.090 --> 00:14:48.590
There mend matters, then venture afar."

00:14:48.590 --> 00:14:50.300
What's that mean?

00:14:50.300 --> 00:14:52.010
Hmm?

00:14:52.010 --> 00:14:54.220
Well, let's see...

00:14:54.220 --> 00:15:02.270
To help people, you first have to help
your family and those close by.

00:15:02.270 --> 00:15:05.150
"Milk Distribution Center"

00:15:02.270 --> 00:15:05.150
Eventually that becomes helping
your country and its people.

00:15:05.150 --> 00:15:08.110
"Canteen" "Curry Rice" "Beef Noodles"

00:15:05.150 --> 00:15:08.110
Eventually that becomes helping
your country and its people.

00:15:08.320 --> 00:15:11.910
Does helping my mom count?

00:15:11.910 --> 00:15:14.780
Sure. That's a fine thing to do.

00:15:14.780 --> 00:15:16.080
I'll do it, too!

00:15:16.080 --> 00:15:17.500
So will I!

00:15:17.500 --> 00:15:18.830
Me, too!

00:15:18.830 --> 00:15:20.420
And me! And me!

00:15:22.380 --> 00:15:26.630
That's right: now everyone's looking
for something they can do.

00:15:26.630 --> 00:15:29.970
So we can all bounce back again--together.

00:15:37.020 --> 00:15:38.930
"One Month Later"

00:15:43.270 --> 00:15:48.320
Ahh... that hot spring felt amazing.

00:15:48.320 --> 00:15:51.400
It must be nice to have one so nearby!

00:15:51.400 --> 00:15:54.490
And only the villagers know about it.

00:15:54.490 --> 00:15:59.000
Still, who knew Yuzu-<i>chan</i>
was so big on top?

00:15:59.000 --> 00:16:02.790
Hey, I bet she'd look great in Western
clothes--like a wedding dress!

00:16:04.210 --> 00:16:08.210
Oh, yeah! Tamahiko would <i>love </i>that!

00:16:08.210 --> 00:16:11.550
I can practically see
his blushing face now!

00:16:12.720 --> 00:16:14.010
Come on!

00:16:14.010 --> 00:16:15.850
Will you please <i>help </i>already?!

00:16:15.850 --> 00:16:17.760
Yes, ma'am!

00:16:17.760 --> 00:16:19.770
This really is relaxing.

00:16:19.770 --> 00:16:22.100
Mmm. But...

00:16:22.100 --> 00:16:25.650
Shiratori-<i>kun</i>, shouldn't you
take off your glasses?

00:16:27.230 --> 00:16:30.740
These glasses are part
of my beautiful face.

00:16:30.740 --> 00:16:33.990
Besides, I want to take in
this mountain scenery!

00:16:33.990 --> 00:16:36.070
What the--I can't see!

00:16:45.790 --> 00:16:47.290
Okay, I'm getting out.

00:16:47.290 --> 00:16:50.420
Tamahiko-<i>sensei</i>!

00:16:50.420 --> 00:16:54.180
Stay and relax a little longer!

00:16:54.180 --> 00:16:55.140
What?!

00:16:55.140 --> 00:16:58.470
Tamahiko-<i>sensei</i>!

00:16:58.470 --> 00:16:59.310
Huh?

00:17:04.560 --> 00:17:05.940
Hey, Yuzu...

00:17:05.940 --> 00:17:06.940
Yes?

00:17:08.940 --> 00:17:13.190
I did something truly awful
when we first met.

00:17:14.530 --> 00:17:15.740
I'm sorry!

00:17:18.240 --> 00:17:19.370
Ryo-<i>san</i>...

00:17:19.370 --> 00:17:24.210
I... I was bought for money once, too.

00:17:24.210 --> 00:17:28.630
I came so close to losing
something precious.

00:17:28.630 --> 00:17:33.470
I saw you looking so happy...
and thought how different we had it.

00:17:34.380 --> 00:17:37.930
You don't have to forgive me. But--

00:17:39.300 --> 00:17:44.180
There's nothing to forgive.
I already like you a lot!

00:17:44.180 --> 00:17:47.810
Besides, remember what you
said at the first-aid site?

00:17:47.810 --> 00:17:51.400
Tamahiko-<i>sama </i>and I are your friends.

00:17:52.480 --> 00:17:55.200
Right... that. That was, um...

00:17:59.070 --> 00:18:02.540
"menacing intensifies"

00:17:59.070 --> 00:18:02.540
Sure looks fun in your
own little world there.

00:18:06.710 --> 00:18:09.330
We <i>happen </i>to be engaged
in secret girl-talk!

00:18:09.330 --> 00:18:12.920
<i>I </i>want secret girl-talk with Yuzu, <i>too</i>!

00:18:12.920 --> 00:18:15.550
Well, <i>I'm </i>basically Yuzu's big sister!

00:18:15.550 --> 00:18:18.930
Threatening me from down there?
You don't scare me.

00:18:21.300 --> 00:18:23.890
You two were <i>made </i>for each other!

00:18:23.890 --> 00:18:26.520
But shouldn't they be back any minute?

00:18:26.520 --> 00:18:28.400
Oh, that's right!

00:18:30.310 --> 00:18:33.190
They loosened me up, all right...

00:18:38.200 --> 00:18:40.160
Welcome home!

00:18:42.660 --> 00:18:44.700
Tamahiko-<i>sensei</i>!

00:18:44.700 --> 00:18:48.290
Happy birthday!

00:18:48.290 --> 00:18:49.290
Huh?

00:18:51.960 --> 00:18:54.630
I know it's terribly late,

00:18:54.630 --> 00:18:56.920
but I'm so glad we can finally celebrate!

00:18:56.920 --> 00:18:57.800
Yuzu...

00:18:57.800 --> 00:19:01.890
We did all the planning in secret--
we wanted to surprise you.

00:19:01.890 --> 00:19:05.140
And we all pitched in on the cooking.

00:19:05.140 --> 00:19:07.350
For me?

00:19:07.350 --> 00:19:11.860
Thanks for lending us your house,
Tamahiko-<i>sensei</i>.

00:19:11.860 --> 00:19:16.190
I bet the grown-ups are
secretly grateful, too.

00:19:16.190 --> 00:19:19.740
The village is bouncing back
faster than we thought, too.

00:19:19.740 --> 00:19:21.450
And it's all thanks to you!

00:19:22.620 --> 00:19:25.870
I'm the one who should be thanking <i>you</i>.

00:19:25.870 --> 00:19:28.910
I heard you all worked really hard.

00:19:28.910 --> 00:19:31.880
Thanks for holding up your
end of our promise.

00:19:36.590 --> 00:19:37.590
Tamako?

00:19:38.670 --> 00:19:43.550
As your brother, I was so proud when
you decided to become a doctor.

00:19:45.010 --> 00:19:50.440
Seeing your resolve made me realize
I had to take action, too.

00:19:50.440 --> 00:19:51.440
Thanks.

00:19:56.480 --> 00:19:57.480
Kotori-<i>chan</i>.

00:19:58.400 --> 00:20:03.030
Your songs provided so much
encouragement for my transfer exam.

00:20:03.030 --> 00:20:04.030
Thank you.

00:20:05.450 --> 00:20:07.580
And thank <i>you</i>, too!

00:20:07.580 --> 00:20:08.410
Ryo.

00:20:09.870 --> 00:20:14.670
Thanks for joining me along
the uneasy road to Tokyo.

00:20:17.380 --> 00:20:18.210
Yuzu?

00:20:19.170 --> 00:20:20.420
Y-Yes?

00:20:21.300 --> 00:20:24.680
Thank you so much for being alive.

00:20:27.350 --> 00:20:29.140
Uh-huh!

00:20:29.140 --> 00:20:30.850
And me? What about me?

00:20:32.560 --> 00:20:34.690
Shiratori-<i>kun</i>.

00:20:34.690 --> 00:20:38.530
Thank you for being my friend.

00:20:41.860 --> 00:20:46.570
Wow! I've never seen that look
on Hakaru-<i>kun</i>'s face before!

00:20:46.570 --> 00:20:50.950
All right: this calls for a song!

00:20:52.330 --> 00:20:54.330
--Hooray!
--Kotori-<i>chan</i>!

00:20:54.330 --> 00:20:56.710
C'mon, everybody--join in!

00:21:08.970 --> 00:21:12.770
<i>Beloved heart, a flower opens</i>

00:21:12.770 --> 00:21:17.690
<i>Two flowers of love</i>

00:21:17.690 --> 00:21:21.480
<i>Beloved heart, your love</i>

00:21:21.480 --> 00:21:26.410
<i>A flower blooms in grace</i>

00:21:26.410 --> 00:21:30.200
<i>Beloved heart, spring rain</i>

00:21:30.200 --> 00:21:35.170
<i>The flower of love in bloom</i>

00:21:35.170 --> 00:21:38.960
<i>Beloved heart, for you</i>

00:21:38.960 --> 00:21:43.300
<i>A flower blooms eternal</i>

00:21:43.300 --> 00:21:47.680
<i>See the wind blow: swaying, swaying</i>

00:21:47.680 --> 00:21:52.020
<i>See it dance: floating, floating</i>

00:21:52.020 --> 00:21:56.940
<i>Now fly to your town:</i>

00:21:56.940 --> 00:21:59.900
<i>Flutter, flutter</i>

00:21:59.900 --> 00:22:05.650
<i>Madly in love, enveloped in your hands</i>

00:22:05.650 --> 00:22:09.450
<i>The flower language of tender feelings</i>

00:22:09.450 --> 00:22:13.870
<i>I want to give the world</i>

00:22:13.870 --> 00:22:17.420
<i>A rainbow of flowers</i>

00:22:17.420 --> 00:22:21.340
<i>And a song of love</i>

00:22:36.770 --> 00:22:38.480
I'll be honest:

00:22:39.650 --> 00:22:42.900
I'm in love with you, Tamahiko-<i>sama</i>.

00:22:42.900 --> 00:22:45.150
You're my first love.

00:22:45.150 --> 00:22:49.610
I had so many regrets after what happened.

00:22:49.610 --> 00:22:53.280
Like... I should have
told you that I loved you.

00:22:53.280 --> 00:22:54.120
I...

00:22:54.910 --> 00:22:58.710
I wanted more kisses--and hand-holding!

00:22:58.710 --> 00:23:03.130
I knew it was vulgar for
a girl to think such things,

00:23:03.130 --> 00:23:05.170
but I couldn't stop.

00:23:06.460 --> 00:23:09.340
There's nothing vulgar here.

00:23:09.340 --> 00:23:12.100
I think of you as a pure maiden.

00:23:12.100 --> 00:23:17.180
I'm glad you found the
chaste romance of a first love.

00:23:19.060 --> 00:23:20.560
Isn't it amazing?

00:23:20.560 --> 00:23:23.480
A person may face all
manner of hopelessness,

00:23:23.480 --> 00:23:25.440
but if someone's there to support them,

00:23:25.440 --> 00:23:28.780
they can bounce right back.

00:23:28.780 --> 00:23:34.030
Someday, I'd like to be the kind
of person who lives for others, too.

00:23:36.290 --> 00:23:43.420
But for that to happen, I've learned
that I need to cherish you first, so...
